# Trivy ignore list (Task 102) — EMPTY BY DEFAULT, and it stays that way
# unless a finding has been reviewed and written up here in this format:
#
#   <CVE-ID>  # <date> <reviewer>: <why this cannot be acted on yet> — <ticket>
#
# The review bar: an unfixed upstream with no exploit path in OUR deployment
# (e.g. a vulnerability in a CLI we never invoke), or a fix that would break
# a pinned contract with a tracked ticket to revisit it. "Noisy" is not a
# reason. Every entry must carry a ticket, and the security workflow's
# misconfig scan reads this file.
